@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# Background Agent cancellation
+
+The existing RuntimeTaskRegistry, child AbortController and Session event/notification owners
+retain their responsibilities. Execution-local settlement state coordinates writes; it is not
+another task store or queue.
+
+```text
+accepted Stop → cancel owned child → serialized output/notification/terminal receipts
+             → registry terminal settlement → release execution-local coordination
+I/O failure → retain retry plan + reject caller; never restore a live child
+```
+
+Concurrent Stop shares the current run's settlement. Failed stages are retryable without a second
+notification; late child completion cannot overwrite a stopped or resumed run. Ordinary completed,
+failed and foreground runs release temporary state. Known committed completion stays completed.
+Reusing its task ID waits for its prior receipt writer, rechecks the same registry, and uses the
+existing Started event before the new execution.
+
+Acceptance uses TaskStop → strict Runtime → real runner/registry/events, a disposable process,
+artifact/queue/event failures, concurrent requests, late completion and completed-result preservation.
+Cancellation requests are not proof of every native executor's termination. Lost acknowledgement
+after committed receipt and cold reconstruction remain separate recovery work; no schema, store,
+permission grant, new UI or exactly-once claim is introduced.
